  "summary": "Harden Tdarr container-stress media handling by synthesizing REMUX-AV timestamps, preserving ambiguous source video packet probes, and projecting source-failure marker codes/retryability into worker result evidence.",
  "reason": "Full Tdarr proof-pack validation exposed WMV timestamp stream-copy failures, false video-missing source rejects when ffprobe omitted nb_read_packets, and invalid AVI/rawvideo failures that were being retried with blank worker-result error codes.",
  "affected_areas": [
    "docs",
    "generated_context",
    "pipeline",
    "tests"
  ],
  "behavior_before": "REMUX-AV could fail on valid WMV/H.264 sources with unset packet timestamps, source route probing treated missing nb_read_packets as zero packets, and corrupt AVI/rawvideo encode failures were recorded as transient retries with blank worker_result.json error codes.",
  "behavior_after": "REMUX-AV adds input-side -fflags +genpts, ambiguous packet-count probes remain eligible while explicit zero-packet probes still fail, and non-retryable source-media FFmpeg failures are recorded and surfaced as terminal source failures with stable error codes.",
